fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.12. Shortcuts now actually work on Android. 0.10.10
    shipped the phrase table inside the APK and taught the engine to look for it in
    the data directory, but PingZhuImeService.ensureData() only extracted the two
    model files — so the table was present and never readable. The engine found
    nothing, silently, and typing a shortcut did nothing.

    The extraction is now one helper for all three files, with deliberate
    differences: the model files are re-extracted when missing, shortcuts.tsv is
    extracted only when absent and never overwritten (the user is meant to edit
    it), and its absence from the APK is not an error.

    Verified on the emulator: all three files land in filesDir/data/.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:45:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.11. The layouts are now published by the engine
    rather than copied into each shell. The seven names used to live in four
    places: the core, and the Windows, Android and HarmonyOS menus. That shape
    of defect is what made the phrase table silent on Android in 0.10.9 — add a
    layout and one menu omits it, or offers a name the engine rejects and falls
    back silently.

    Also in this release:

    - engine_layout_rows() on the C ABI, "id:label" per line, in menu order.
    - The Windows config no longer opens the DLL itself to validate the ini's
      layout; the caller passes the list in, which also lets the config tests
      run without a linked engine.
    - TSF DLL renamed to pingzhu-tsf-0.10.11.dll: this release does change the
      files compiled into it.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 00:35:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.10. Shortcuts now work on Android. 0.10.9 claimed the
    feature needed no shell changes; that held for five of the six front ends.
    Android builds its engine through its own Rust entry point (nativeCreate) rather
    than the C ABI, and that one still called Dictionary::load — so the phrase table
    was read everywhere except the phone, silently, with no error anywhere.

    Also in this release:

    - The android/rust crate had no tests at all; it now has two that pin the rule.
    - Two documentation fixes from the Code Review PR on AtomGit: docs/06 said "six
      front ends" where it means five shells plus the web demo, and the README had no
      user-facing description of shortcuts at all.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 10:05:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.9. Shortcuts: a plain-text phrase table, read from
    data/shortcuts.tsv. A shortcut is not a second kind of thing — it is an entry
    in the same format whose score sorts it first, so no new ABI and no new UI
    were needed. Phrases are read-only and never take part in learning.

    Also in this release:

    - The three packaging lists that name data files (Windows, Android, HarmonyOS)
      now carry shortcuts.tsv. The deb and rpm already did, because they install
      the whole data directory.
    - HarmonyOS: a listed file missing from rawfile no longer throws.
    - RELEASING.md: the TSF DLL rename rule is now keyed to the files compiled
      into the DLL, not to everything under windows/. This release changed
      windows/package.sh, which does not alter the DLL, so the name is unchanged.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:15:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.8. A syllable typed without its tone now works:
    most Bopomofo users leave the tone out, and the last syllable used to stay
    pending — nothing was committed at all. It is now expanded into the four tones
    and the language model picks.

    Also in this release:

    - A harness round-trip check compared tones, which silently dropped 48 samples
      once the decoder began choosing a tone. It compares syllable boundaries now.
    - The benchmark reports the honest distribution: top-1 76.80% rather than
      78.82%, because tone-less readings are counted instead of filtered out. The
      2,413 toned readings score exactly as before.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.7. Punctuation has a page on the phone shells now:
    every key on a Bopomofo layout is a reading (`,` is ㄝ), and a phone has no
    Shift to reach a comma with. The table lives in the engine, so the shells and
    the demo page show the same page rather than one copy each.

    Also in this release:

    - Android: the input window covered the whole screen, so the application's
      window measured zero pixels and drew nothing — the user could not see what
      they typed.
    - Android and HarmonyOS: a character the layout has no key for was dropped
      instead of being sent to the editor.
    - The demo page's board did not fit a phone, and its build silently left out a
      module the page imported.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:45:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.6. The engine now has seven keyboard layouts
    (standard, eten, hsu, eten26, ibm, ginyieh, mitac), transcribed from the
    reference implementation by a generator rather than by hand, and every front
    end can choose one: Windows and Linux read a file, macOS a menu, Android the
    settings screen, HarmonyOS a long press on the script key, the demo page a
    picker above the keyboard.

    Also in this release:

    - The drawn keyboard was a second copy of the layout in the Android and
      HarmonyOS shells, so choosing a layout decoded one way and drew another.
    - HarmonyOS could not produce a single Latin letter, could not switch the
      output script, and never showed the sentence it would commit.
    - Linux could toggle the output script only by editing its file, not with
      the Ctrl+Alt+S the other shells have.
    - The demo page forgot the words a user taught it when the tab closed.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:50:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.5. Two fixes, both of the shape "the feature is
    there, the result is empty":

    - Selecting a candidate committed nothing on Android and macOS: select()
      already commits and returns the text, and those shells asked the engine to
      commit again, which returns nothing.
    - This addon and the HarmonyOS keyboard never wrote the user dictionary, so
      every word the user taught was forgotten on restart. They now load it at
      startup and write it after a selection or a commit, like the other shells.

 -- PingZhu <173787247@qq.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0800

fcitx5-pingzhu (0.10.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.10.4. Four shells each had a feature that existed but
    could not be reached: Android's candidate row never appeared at all and its
    candidate list could not be opened, HarmonyOS's backspace threw the whole
    composition away and deleted a character as well, Linux could not page past
    the first ten candidates, and Windows's candidate window cut off its own
    status line. The addon's own Version= in linux/fcitx5/pingzhu.conf now
    follows the release number — it had said 0.9.0 since 0.9.0, because the
    VERSION in CMakeLists.txt is a value nothing reads.

